<title>UK: Brown says consumer spending likely to stay strong.</title>
<headline>Brown says consumer spending likely to stay strong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said in his budget speech on Wednesday British consumer spending is likely to remain strong.</p>
<p>&quot;We have seen a rapid growth of consumer spending, of nearly four percent over the last year,&quot; he told parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;With the prospect of further windfalls from the building societies, consumer spending is likely to remain strong.&quot;</p>
<p>Economists are worried that a flood of windfall payments from building societies converting into banks -- totalling more than 30 billion pounds over the summer -- will fuel an unsustainable high street boom.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708 +44 171 542 7708</p>
